@startuml Sequence_Dropout_Reconnection
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Client1 as "Client 1 (Healthy)"
actor Client2 as "Client 2 (Drops out / Reconnects)"
participant Gateway as "FastAPI Gateway"
participant Coordinator as "Coordinator State Machine"
database DB as "PostgreSQL"

== Round t: Client 2 Drops Out ==
Coordinator -> Coordinator : Round t State = OPEN / COLLECTING
Client1 -> Gateway : POST /update (Round t update)
Gateway -> DB : Save update from Client 1

Note over Client2 : Client 2 experiences network failure / crashes\n(No update received)

Coordinator -> Coordinator : Round t Deadline Reached (Timeout)
Coordinator -> DB : Query received updates count
alt Count >= min_participants (Quorum Met without Client 2)
    Coordinator -> DB : Mark Client 2 as "DROPOUT" for Round t
    Coordinator -> Coordinator : Aggregate with Client 1 updates only
    Coordinator -> DB : Complete Round t successfully
    Coordinator -> Coordinator : Open Round t + 1
else Count < min_participants (Quorum Failed)
    Coordinator -> DB : Mark Round t as FAILED (Quorum not met)
    Coordinator -> Coordinator : Retry Round t
end

== Round t+1: Client 2 Reconnects ==
Client2 -> Client2 : Network restored / Client restarts
Client2 -> Gateway : GET /task (client_id=Client2)
Gateway -> Coordinator : Query current round
Coordinator --> Gateway : Active Round is t + 1
Gateway --> Client2 : TaskAssignment (round_id=t+1, new global model version)

Client2 -> Gateway : GET /model/{run_id}/{version=t+1}
Gateway --> Client2 : Model weights v_{t+1}
Note over Client2 : Client 2 synchronizes to newest model\nand resumes regular training
Client2 -> Gateway : POST /update (Round t+1 update)
Gateway --> Client2 : 200 OK (Accepted)
@enduml
